jinja: compute the integer +, -, * and % in int64_t, with errors for a zero divisor and an overflow
Fold-into: upstream/common

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 plus every patch of the series before this one.

The binary operators of two integers computed in double and cast the result
back with static_cast<int64_t>. For "{{ 1 % 0 }}", fmod gives NaN, and the
cast of NaN is undefined: UBSan reports a float-cast-overflow at
common/jinja/runtime.cpp in test-jinja ("arithmetic edge cases"), in debug
and release. For "{{ 999999999999999999 * 999999999999999999 }}", the
product is outside int64_t, and that cast is also undefined. The double path
also loses the exact value of an integer past 2^53.

The change: two integers use int64_t arithmetic. A zero divisor of % throws
"Integer modulo by zero" (Jinja raises ZeroDivisionError). A result outside
int64_t throws "Integer overflow" (Python gives a larger integer, which
int64_t cannot hold). INT64_MIN % -1 gives 0. The sign of % stays the sign of
the dividend, as the fmod of the float path. The float operators do not
change.

test-jinja gets the case "integer arithmetic past 2^53", which also runs
against Python Jinja2 in test-jinja -py, and the case "integer errors".
test-jinja and test-jinja -py pass with no report in none and ubsan, debug
and release.

